<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">keep on walking, come what will</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;â€œArenâ€™t you twoâ€”â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œIf youâ€™re done talking about Adora and Catra getting married,â€ says Entrapta, with all the subtlety and tact of a sledgehammer, â€œI have calculated the voltage neededâ€¦â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Wherever the rest of Entraptaâ€™s sentence is going to go, it falls away. The whole room falls away as understanding hits Catra like a bolt of lightning, an electrifying shock to her system that leaves her reeling. &lt;i&gt;Getting married&lt;/i&gt;? Her and &lt;i&gt;Adora&lt;/i&gt;? Questions well up on her tongue â€” &lt;i&gt;What? Why?&lt;/i&gt; â€” and she doesnâ€™t realize she has fumbled through those fragmented inquiries until Frosta answers her.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œUm. Youâ€™re wearing Adoraâ€™s pin.â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;center&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;__________________&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/center&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Adora and Catra get engaged. If only someone would tell them.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
